.SH NAME
.PP
waybar \- mango layout module
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBlayout\fR module displays the current layout symbol of the monitor (e.\&g.\& "S", "M") in the Mango compositor.\&
It supports dynamic CSS classes and custom formats based on the active layout symbol.\&
.PP
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Addressed by \fBmango/layout\fR
.PP
\fBformat\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: {} 
.br
The default format, how the layout symbol should be displayed.\& The positional \fB{}\fR (the default) and \fB{symbol}\fR are both replaced by the current layout symbol.\&
.PP
\fBformat\-<symbol>\fR: 
.br
typeof: string 
.br
default: \fBnone\fR 
.br
The custom format to use when a specific layout symbol is active (e.\&g.\&, \fBformat\-S\fR, \fBformat\-M\fR).\& Note that the symbol string is strictly case\-sensitive.\& If no match is found, it falls back to \fBformat\fR.\&
.PP
\fBexpand\fR: 
.br
typeof: bool 
.br
default: false 
.br
Enables the module to consume all leftover space.\&
.PP
.SH FORMAT REPLACEMENTS
.PP
\fB{symbol}\fR: The layout symbol reported by Mango (e.\&g.\&, "S", "M", "Dwindle").\&
.PP
.SH CUSTOM FORMATS
.PP
You can define specific formats for different layouts by appending the exact layout symbol to the \fBformat\-\fR key in your configuration.\&
.PP
For example, if your Mango compositor reports the symbol "S" for a spiral layout and "M" for a master layout, you can use \fBformat\-S\fR and \fBformat\-M\fR to define unique icons or text for each.\& Keep in mind that JSON keys are case\-sensitive, so if the compositor sends "S", the key must be exactly \fBformat\-S\fR.\&
.PP
.SH STYLE
.PP
The layout module provides dynamic CSS classes based on the current layout symbol, allowing you to style each layout differently.\&
.PP
\fB \fR#layout\fB
\fR \fB.\&<symbol>\fR \- The current layout symbol is dynamically added as a CSS class name (e.\&g.\&, \fB.\&S\fR, \fB.\&M\fR).\&
.PP
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"mango/layout": {
    "format": "[] {symbol}",
    "format\-S": "󰌌 {symbol}",
    "format\-M": "󰕰 {symbol}"
}
.fi
.RE
.PP
.SS CSS Example
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
#layout {
    color: #ffffff;
    padding: 0 5px;
}

/* Specific color for the "S" layout */
#layout\&.S {
    color: #a6e3a1;
}

/* Specific color for the "M" layout */
#layout\&.M {
    color: #f38ba8;
}
.fi
.RE
